theory.intro:
Heights and distances that are awkward to measure can be found using **similar triangles**. A tall object and a short stick or person cast shadows in the same sunlight, forming two triangles with equal angles.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (1.5,0);
\coordinate (T) at (1.5,0.6);
\coordinate (C) at (5.4,0);
\coordinate (S) at (5.4,2.16);
\draw (O) -- (C);
\draw (B) -- (T);
\draw (C) -- (S);
\draw (O) -- (S);
\coordinate (b1) at ($(B)!0.25cm!(O)$);
\coordinate (b2) at ($(B)!0.25cm!(T)$);
\draw (b1) -- ($(b1)+(b2)-(B)$) -- (b2);
\coordinate (c1) at ($(C)!0.25cm!(O)$);
\coordinate (c2) at ($(C)!0.25cm!(S)$);
\draw (c1) -- ($(c1)+(c2)-(C)$) -- (c2);
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.55cm] {angle = C--O--S};
\node[right] at (1.5,0.3) {$h$};
\node[right] at (5.4,1.08) {$H$};
\draw[<->] (0,-0.55) -- (1.5,-0.55) node[midway,below] {$d$};
\draw[<->] (0,-1.35) -- (5.4,-1.35) node[midway,below] {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
A vertical post $1.5$ m high casts a shadow $2.5$ m long. At the same time, a tree casts a shadow $10$ m long on level ground. Find the height $h$ of the tree. The diagrams are not drawn to scale.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(2,0)--(0,1.2)--cycle;
\draw (0.18,0)--(0.18,0.18)--(0,0.18);
\node[left] at (0,0.6) {$1.5\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (1,0) {$2.5\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (1,1.4) {Post};
\draw (3.5,0)--(6.5,0)--(3.5,1.8)--cycle;
\draw (3.68,0)--(3.68,0.18)--(3.5,0.18);
\node[left] at (3.5,0.9) {$h$};
\node[below] at (5,0) {$10\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (5,2) {Tree};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A person stands $8$ m from a vertical lamp post and casts a shadow $2$ m long on level ground. The lamp is $7$ m above the ground. Find the person's height $h$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(5,0)--(5,3.5)--cycle;
\draw (1,0)--(1,0.7);
\draw (0.82,0)--(0.82,0.18)--(1,0.18);
\draw (4.82,0)--(4.82,0.18)--(5,0.18);
\node[left] at (1,0.45) {$h$};
\node[right] at (5,1.75) {$7\text{ m}$};
\draw[<->] (0,-0.5)--(1,-0.5) node[midway,below] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw[<->] (1,-0.5)--(5,-0.5) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ m}$};
\node[above left] at (0,0) {Shadow tip};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two cables support a vertical pole on level ground at the same angle. The cables are $6$ m and $15$ m long. The shorter cable reaches $4$ m up the pole; the longer cable reaches its top. Find the pole's height $h$. The diagram is not drawn to scale.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-3.354,0)--(0,0)--(0,3);
\draw (-3.354,0)--(0,3) node[midway,above left] {$15\text{ m}$};
\draw (-1.342,0)--(0,1.2) node[midway,above left] {$6\text{ m}$};
\draw (-0.18,0)--(-0.18,0.18)--(0,0.18);
\draw[<->] (0.45,0)--(0.45,1.2) node[midway,right] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw[<->] (1.6,0)--(1.6,3) node[midway,right] {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A surveyor uses two similar triangles to find the width $w$ of a chasm. Points $A$, $B$ and $C$ lie on one straight line, and points $D$, $B$ and $E$ lie on another. The marked angles at $A$ and $C$ are right angles. Find $w$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (1.2,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.8,0);
\coordinate (D) at (0,-0.8);
\coordinate (E) at (4.8,2.4);
\draw (A)--(C);
\draw (A)--(D);
\draw (C)--(E);
\draw[dashed] (D)--(E);
\draw (0,-0.18)--(0.18,-0.18)--(0.18,0);
\draw (4.62,0)--(4.62,0.18)--(4.8,0.18);
\node[above] at (0.6,0) {$3\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (3,0) {$9\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,-0.4) {$2\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (4.8,1.2) {$w$};
\node[above left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above right,xshift=3mm,yshift=3mm] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\node[above] at (E) {$E$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A person $2$ m tall and a vertical flagpole $10$ m high cast shadows in the same sunlight on level ground. The flagpole's shadow is $12$ m longer than the person's shadow. Find the person's shadow length $d$. The diagrams are not drawn to scale; lengths are in metres.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(1.8,0)--(0,1.2)--cycle;
\draw (0.18,0)--(0.18,0.18)--(0,0.18);
\node[left] at (0,0.6) {$2$};
\node[below] at (0.9,0) {$d$};
\node[above] at (0.9,1.4) {Person};
\draw (3.5,0)--(6.5,0)--(3.5,2)--cycle;
\draw (3.68,0)--(3.68,0.18)--(3.5,0.18);
\node[left] at (3.5,1) {$10$};
\node[below] at (5,0) {$d+12$};
\node[above] at (5,2.2) {Flagpole};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
A $1$ m vertical stick casts a shadow $2$ m long.
At the same time a tree casts a shadow $8$ m long.
Find the height of the tree.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,1.2);
\draw (0,0) -- (2.4,0) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ m}$};
\draw (2.4,0) -- (0,1.2);
\node[left] at (0,0.6) {$h$};
\draw (3.4,0) -- (3.4,0.3);
\draw (3.4,0) -- (4.0,0) node[midway,below] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw (4.0,0) -- (3.4,0.3);
\node[left] at (3.4,0.15) {$1\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A $1$ m vertical stick casts a shadow $1.5$ m long.
At the same time a building casts a shadow $9$ m long.
Find the height of the building.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,1.6);
\draw (0,0) -- (2.4,0) node[midway,below] {$9\text{ m}$};
\draw (2.4,0) -- (0,1.6);
\node[left] at (0,0.8) {$h$};
\draw (3.4,0) -- (3.4,0.27);
\draw (3.4,0) -- (3.8,0) node[midway,below] {$1.5\text{ m}$};
\draw (3.8,0) -- (3.4,0.27);
\node[left] at (3.4,0.135) {$1\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A person $1.6$ m tall casts a shadow $2$ m long.
At the same time a tree casts a shadow $5$ m long.
Find the height of the tree.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,1.92);
\draw (0,0) -- (2.4,0) node[midway,below] {$5\text{ m}$};
\draw (2.4,0) -- (0,1.92);
\node[left] at (0,0.96) {$h$};
\draw (3.4,0) -- (3.4,0.77);
\draw (3.4,0) -- (4.36,0) node[midway,below] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw (4.36,0) -- (3.4,0.77);
\node[left] at (3.4,0.38) {$1.6\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A vertical flagpole and a $1$ m vertical ruler cast shadows in the same sunlight.
The ruler's shadow is $0.8$ m long and the flagpole's shadow is $4.8$ m long.
Find the height of the flagpole.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,1.92);
\draw (0,0) -- (1.536,0) node[midway,below] {$4.8\text{ m}$};
\draw (1.536,0) -- (0,1.92);
\node[left] at (0,0.96) {$h$};
\draw (2.5,0) -- (2.5,0.32);
\draw (2.5,0) -- (2.756,0) node[midway,below] {$0.8\text{ m}$};
\draw (2.756,0) -- (2.5,0.32);
\node[left] at (2.5,0.16) {$1\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A $12$ m tree casts a shadow $8$ m long.
At the same time a bush beside it casts a shadow $2$ m long.
Find the height of the bush.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,2.4);
\draw (0,0) -- (1.6,0) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ m}$};
\draw (1.6,0) -- (0,2.4);
\node[left] at (0,1.2) {$12\text{ m}$};
\draw (2.6,0) -- (2.6,0.6);
\draw (2.6,0) -- (3.0,0) node[midway,below] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw (3.0,0) -- (2.6,0.6);
\node[left] at (2.6,0.3) {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The figures represent a vertical tree and a $2$ m vertical post casting shadows on level ground in the same sunlight.
Find the height of the tree.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,1.92);
\draw (0,0) -- (2.4,0) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ m}$};
\draw (2.4,0) -- (0,1.92);
\node[left] at (0,0.96) {$h$};
\draw (3.4,0) -- (3.4,0.48);
\draw (3.4,0) -- (4.0,0) node[midway,below] {$2.5\text{ m}$};
\draw (4.0,0) -- (3.4,0.48);
\node[left] at (3.4,0.24) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
A light pole has a globe $6$ m above the ground.
A boy stands $10$ m from the base of the pole and casts a shadow $2$ m long.
Find the height of the boy.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0.7,0) node[midway,below] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw (0.7,0) -- (4.2,0) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,0) -- (4.2,2.1);
\draw (0.7,0) -- (0.7,0.35);
\draw (4.2,0) -- (4.2,2.1) node[midway,right] {$6\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0.7,0.2) {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A street lamp is $5$ m high.
When a girl stands $6$ m from the base of the lamp her shadow is $1.8$ m long.
Find the height of the girl, to the nearest centimetre.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0.9,0) node[midway,below] {$1.8\text{ m}$};
\draw (0.9,0) -- (3.9,0) node[midway,below] {$6\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,0) -- (3.9,2.5);
\draw (0.9,0) -- (0.9,0.577);
\draw (3.9,0) -- (3.9,2.5) node[midway,right] {$5\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0.9,0.29) {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two cables support a vertical pole at the same angle.
The cables are $4$ m and $10$ m long, and the shorter cable reaches $3$ m up the pole.
Find the height of the pole.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (-2.1166,0) -- (0,0);
\draw (0,0) -- (0,2.4);
\draw[gray] (0.22,0) -- (0.22,0.96) node[midway,right] {$3\text{ m}$};
\draw (-2.1166,0) -- (0,2.4) node[midway,above left] {$10\text{ m}$};
\draw (-0.8467,0) -- (0,0.96) node[midway,above left] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw (-0.15,0) -- (-0.15,0.15) -- (0,0.15);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

James is $1.7$ m tall and casts a shadow $2$ m long.
At the same time a tower casts a shadow $13$ m long.
Find the height of the tower.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,2.04);
\draw (0,0) -- (2.4,0) node[midway,below] {$13\text{ m}$};
\draw (2.4,0) -- (0,2.04);
\node[left] at (0,1.02) {$h$};
\draw (3.4,0) -- (3.4,0.314);
\draw (3.4,0) -- (3.769,0) node[midway,below] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw (3.769,0) -- (3.4,0.314);
\node[left] at (3.4,0.157) {$1.7\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two cables support a vertical pole at the same angle.
The cables are $3$ m and $9$ m long, and the shorter cable reaches $2$ m up the pole.
Find the height of the pole.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (-2.1466,0) -- (0,0);
\draw (0,0) -- (0,1.92);
\draw[gray] (0.22,0) -- (0.22,0.64) node[midway,right] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw (-2.1466,0) -- (0,1.92) node[midway,above left] {$9\text{ m}$};
\draw (-0.7155,0) -- (0,0.64) node[midway,above left] {$3\text{ m}$};
\draw (-0.15,0) -- (-0.15,0.15) -- (0,0.15);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A rock sits across a chasm.
Pegs are placed on the near side to make two similar triangles, as shown.
Find the width $w$ of the chasm.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (-0.4,0) -- (0,0);
\draw (0,0) -- (0.8,0) node[midway,above] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw (0.8,0) -- (4.0,0) node[midway,above] {$8\text{ m}$};
\draw (4.0,0) -- (4.4,0);
\draw (0,0) -- (0,-0.72) node[midway,left] {$1.8\text{ m}$};
\draw (4.0,0) -- (4.0,2.88) node[midway,right] {$w$};
\draw[dashed] (0,-0.72) -- (4.0,2.88);
\draw (3.4,2.88) -- (4.6,2.88);
\node[above right] at (4.0,2.88) {Rock};
\draw (0,-0.15) -- (0.15,-0.15) -- (0.15,0);
\draw (3.85,0) -- (3.85,0.15) -- (4.0,0.15);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.question_text:
A surveyor finds the width $w$ of a river using two similar triangles, as shown.
Find $w$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (-0.4,0) -- (0,0);
\draw (0,0) -- (1.28,0) node[midway,above] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw (1.28,0) -- (5.12,0) node[midway,above] {$12\text{ m}$};
\draw (5.12,0) -- (5.5,0);
\draw (0,0) -- (0,-0.96) node[midway,left] {$3\text{ m}$};
\draw (5.12,0) -- (5.12,2.88) node[midway,right] {$w$};
\draw[dashed] (0,-0.96) -- (5.12,2.88);
\draw (4.5,2.88) -- (5.7,2.88);
\node[above right] at (5.12,2.88) {Tree};
\draw (0,-0.15) -- (0.15,-0.15) -- (0.15,0);
\draw (4.97,0) -- (4.97,0.15) -- (5.12,0.15);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A person $1.8$ m tall stands $4$ m from a lamp post and casts a shadow $2$ m long.
Find the height of the lamp post.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (1.0,0) node[midway,below] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw (1.0,0) -- (3.0,0) node[midway,below] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,0) -- (3.0,2.7);
\draw (1.0,0) -- (1.0,0.9) node[midway,left] {$1.8\text{ m}$};
\draw (3.0,0) -- (3.0,2.7) node[midway,right] {$H$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A person $1.6$ m tall and an $8$ m flagpole cast shadows at the same time.
The flagpole's shadow is $6$ m longer than the person's shadow.
Find the length of the person's shadow.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (0,0.448);
\draw (0,0) -- (0.42,0) node[midway,below] {$d$};
\draw (0.42,0) -- (0,0.448);
\node[left] at (0,0.224) {$1.6\text{ m}$};
\draw (3.0,0) -- (3.0,2.24);
\draw (3.0,0) -- (5.1,0) node[midway,below] {$d+6$};
\draw (5.1,0) -- (3.0,2.24);
\node[left] at (3.0,1.12) {$8\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
